<title>USA: Anika gets European Orthovisc approval.</title>
<headline>Anika gets European Orthovisc approval.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anika Research Inc said on Wednesday it had received the CE mark approval to market its Orthovisc product in Europe.</p>
<p>The CE mark, a certification required under European Community medical device regulation, will allow Orthovisc to be sold without further approvals in most of the 15 EC nations as well as European countries that recognize EC device legislation.</p>
<p>Orthovisc, comprised of hyaluronic acid, a substance found in fluid of joints, relieves pain and improves joint function in patients suffering from osteoartritis.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733.</p>
